<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/11th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Levounion</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1091">1091</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Levounion was fought on 29 April 1091 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thrace">Thrace</a>, near the mouth of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maritsa">Maritsa</a>, between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pechenegs">Pechenegs</a>. Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexios-i-komnenos">Alexios I Komnenos</a>, aided by Cuman allies, destroyed a Pecheneg horde that had threatened <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>, killing most of its warriors and their families. The victory ended the Pecheneg danger to the empire for a generation.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-levounion.jpg" alt="Battle of Levounion" width="320" height="553" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alexius_I.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
